For the general clause of the Example, let $	ilde u=(	ilde u^0,	ilde u_{\mathrm{vec}})$ be any timelike displacement and let $w=(w^0,w_{\mathrm{vec}})
eq0$ satisfy $\eta(	ilde u,w)=0$. Timelikeness gives $\lvert	ilde u^0vert>\lvert	ilde u_{\mathrm{vec}}vert$ by [L1] and [L3], and orthogonality gives $	ilde u_{\mathrm{vec}}\cdot w_{\mathrm{vec}}=	ilde u^0w^0$. Suppose, for contradiction, that $\eta(w,w)\le0$; then $\lvert w_{\mathrm{vec}}vert\le\lvert w^0vert$, and $w_{\mathrm{vec}}
eq0$, because $w_{\mathrm{vec}}=0$ would give $	ilde u^0w^0=0$ and hence $w=0$, contradicting $w
eq0$. Cauchy–Schwarz [L5] now yields the contradictory chain $\lvert	ilde u^0vert\lvert w^0vert=\lvert	ilde u_{\mathrm{vec}}\cdot w_{\mathrm{vec}}vert\le\lvert	ilde u_{\mathrm{vec}}vert\lvert w_{\mathrm{vec}}vert<\lvert	ilde u^0vert\lvert w_{\mathrm{vec}}vert\le\lvert	ilde u^0vert\lvert w^0vert$, where the strict inequality uses $\lvert	ilde u_{\mathrm{vec}}vert<\lvert	ilde u^0vert$ and $w_{\mathrm{vec}}
eq0$ and the last inequality uses $\lvert w_{\mathrm{vec}}vert\le\lvert w^0vert$. Hence $\eta(w,w)>0$, that is, every nonzero displacement orthogonal to a timelike displacement is spacelike by [L3].
